  "rationale": "**Does not hold in general.** `workspace_status` derives states as follows: registry/workspace plugins get `Active` when `Plugin::applies` holds under a context with `used_plugins` (else `Dormant`); dependency-embedded plugins come from `discovery::discover`/`decide` (`Used`/`AutoEnabled` -> active, `Candidate`, `Declined`); `use`d non-dependency crates are `Active`, a `use`d dependency offering no plugin `Dormant`; leftover `disable` names `Declined`. This matches activation in the tested cases, but the final `disable` loop also reports a registry plugin named in `[plugins] disable` as `declined`, while activation ignores `disable` for registry plugins (only discovery and `use` resolution consult `is_disabled`; `skills::active_plugins` does not), so that plugin runs.\n\nReproduced with the built binary: registry plugin `foo` with `disable = [\"foo\"]` is shown both `✅ active` and `➖ declined`; the declined line contradicts activation. Also untested: a `Used`/`AutoEnabled` dependency plugin whose own plugin-level predicates fail is still reported active by `entry_for` (judged from code only).\n\nTests (all pass): `status_reports_candidate_then_used`, `status_reports_dormant_registry_plugin`, `status_reports_a_used_but_disabled_plugin_as_declined`, `status_lists_each_declined_name_once`, `status_reports_a_pluginless_dependency_only_when_used`, and the unit test `undecided_dependency_plugin_is_a_candidate`.",
